       <h1>Chirag Paswan Criticizes Opposition Protests and Outlines UP Election Plans</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Union Minister Chirag Paswan has condemned opposition parties for blocking Delhi roads, arguing that such protests inconvenience citizens rather than resolving political concerns. He urged the opposition to engage in direct dialogue with the Election Commission instead of continuing demonstrations.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-09/chirag-paswan-criticizes-opposition-protests-and-outlines-up.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Separately, Paswan announced that his party, the LJP (Ram Vilas), is preparing to contest all 403 seats in the 2027 Uttar Pradesh Assembly elections. While the party is currently allied with the NDA in Bihar and at the national level, a final decision regarding an alliance for the UP polls has not been determined.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Covers the political commentary and the specific election strategy mentioned in the source accurately.</p>
