     <article class="story single" data-beat="education">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">EDUCATION</span> · Education (aggregate) · 2026-10-09 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>House Panel Recommends NEET-UG Age, Attempt Limits</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#NEET-UG</span> <span>#Education</span> <span>#Eligibility</span></div>
       <p>A House panel has requested the Centre to investigate the implementation of age and attempt restrictions for the National Eligibility cum Entrance Test (NEET-UG). This recommendation, reported by ThePrint, follows observations of candidates exceeding 70 years of age participating in the examination.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-09/house-panel-recommends-neet-ug-age-attempt-limits.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The call for exploring new limits aims to address concerns regarding the eligibility criteria for the medical entrance test. The panel's suggestion highlights a potential need to refine the parameters for prospective NEET-UG candidates.</p><p>What to watch: Further action by the Centre on the panel's recommendations.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately captures the core request of the house panel and provides the necessary context from the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5" rel="noopener">Education (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
