       <h1>IISc Leads Indian Institutions on Stanford's Top 2% Scientists List 2026</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Education</span> <span>#Science</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#IISc</span></div>
       <p>The Indian Institute of Science (IISc) has emerged as the leading Indian institution on Stanford’s World’s Top 2% Scientists List for 2026. The prestigious list recognizes 139 researchers from IISc, highlighting their significant contributions to global scientific research.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-09/iisc-leads-indian-institutions-on-stanfords-top-2-scientists.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>This placement positions IISc at the forefront among Indian institutions, according to News18. The annual list by Stanford University identifies scientists across various fields whose work has demonstrated exceptional influence and impact.</p><p>The inclusion of 139 researchers from IISc underscores the institution's strong research output and its impact on the international scientific community. The 2026 list reaffirms IISc's standing as a hub for scientific excellence in India.</p><p>What to watch: Further recognition for Indian research institutions.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurately reflects the source summary and provides appropriate context.</p>
