     <article class="story single" data-beat="tech">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">TECH</span> · TechCrunch · 2026-10-09 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>LumenUs Platform Automates Administrative Tasks After Death</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#tech</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Founder Sara Tashakorinia has launched LumenUs, an AI-driven platform designed to manage the administrative burdens that follow the death of a loved one. The service helps grieving families navigate complex tasks, such as filing insurance claims, locating tax forms, and closing financial accounts, which can otherwise total hundreds of hours of work.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-09/lumenus-platform-automates-administrative-tasks-after-death.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>LumenUs prioritizes tasks by urgency and identifies potential unclaimed financial benefits to assist users during immediate bereavement. The platform, developed with experts from Google and Box, uses onboarding questionnaires to personalize the experience while maintaining security for sensitive financial and legal information.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurately captures the platform's purpose and the team's professional background.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://techcrunch.com/2026/10/09/lumenus-helps-automate-tedious-paperwork-in-times-of-grief/" rel="noopener">TechCrunch</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
