     <article class="story single" data-beat="positive">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">POSITIVE</span> · The Better India · 2026-10-09 · editor 10/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Nagpur Startup eVerse.AI Deploys 40,000+ Smart Collars for Dairy Farms</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Technology</span> <span>#Agriculture</span> <span>#Innovation</span></div>
       <p>Nagpur-based eVerse.AI, founded in 2022 by Ashish Sonkusare, Shailendra Narwade, and Vidhi Gaur, is transforming dairy farming with AI, IoT, and blockchain technology. The startup has already deployed over 40,000 AI collars, which continuously track a cow's temperature, activity, movement, and behavior. This data is then analyzed by AI and machine learning to identify changes that farmers might otherwise miss.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-09/nagpur-startup-everseai-deploys-40000-smart-collars-for-dair.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The 'Connected Cow Collar' is designed to predict when an animal may fall sick before visible symptoms appear, enabling farmers to seek early veterinary care and reduce serious illness. The technology also accurately detects heat cycles, crucial for timely artificial insemination, sending alerts directly to farmers' phones to improve breeding outcomes. Furthermore, GPS functionality assists farmers in locating animals that wander away while grazing.</p><p>Ankush Shelke, a 35-year-old farmer from Khedi village, has experienced significant improvements in his five-cow dairy since adopting the technology. He now receives heat-cycle and illness alerts and reports that each animal yields an additional 2–3 litres of milk daily. This increased productivity has allowed him to expand his dairy with more cows, buffaloes, and calves. The Connected Cow app stores comprehensive health, medical, and productivity records, complemented by CowGPT, an AI guidance tool on WhatsApp that operates in multiple Indian languages, accepting voice notes or text queries.</p><p>eVerse.AI is also engaged in sustainability efforts through its Maharashtra Methane Mission and Banas Methane Programme, promoting balanced feed to reduce livestock methane emissions and enhance milk yield. These initiatives aim to generate carbon credits, offering participating farmers an additional income stream and connecting climate finance with rural communities. With partnerships including Amul, Banas Dairy, and Mother Dairy, eVerse.AI plans to expand across major dairy states, striving for timely information, healthier cattle, and better incomes for farmers.</p><p>Why it matters: This technology improves animal health and farmer livelihoods while addressing environmental concerns in dairy farming.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The report effectively synthesizes the source material, capturing the startup's technology, impact, and strategic initiatives without missing key details.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://thebetterindia.com/web-stories/innovation/everse-ai-cow-collar-cow-health-dairy-farmers-increase-income-nagpur-india-12659598" rel="noopener">The Better India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/nagpur/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Nagpur</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
