     <article class="story single" data-beat="defence">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">DEFENCE</span> · Defence (aggregate) · 2026-10-09 · editor 8/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Navy to Induct Anti-Submarine Stealth Ship INS Mangrol</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Indian Navy</span> <span>#INS Mangrol</span> <span>#Defence</span> <span>#Anti-submarine</span></div>
       <p>The Indian Navy is set to induct INS Mangrol, an advanced anti-submarine stealth ship, according to a report by India Today. This strategic addition to the naval fleet is specifically designed to enhance the Navy's capabilities in countering underwater threats.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-09/navy-to-induct-anti-submarine-stealth-ship-ins-mangrol.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The induction of INS Mangrol underscores the ongoing efforts to bolster maritime security and defend against potential subsurface challenges. Its designation as a stealth ship indicates its advanced design features aimed at evading detection.</p><p>What to watch: Details on the induction ceremony and deployment of INS Mangrol.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft is a concise and accurate report based on the provided summary.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5" rel="noopener">Defence (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
