       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-09 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>NTR District Hosts 'Operation Trishul' Candle Rally</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Students, police, and various community organizations gathered in Mylavaram, NTR district, for a candle rally as part of 'Operation Trishul'. The event aimed to raise awareness against the dangers of drug abuse and negligent driving.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-09/ntr-district-hosts-operation-trishul-candle-rally.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Deputy Commissioner of Police Lakshmi Narayana and other officials led the march, which included participants from local engineering colleges and NGOs. The rally featured students shouting slogans against substance abuse to educate the public on the risks associated with drugs and reckless behavior on the road.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the event, participants, and purpose as described in the source.</p>
