       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-09 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Pallium India Celebrates World Hospice and Palliative Care Day</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Pallium India is hosting a celebration for World Hospice and Palliative Care Day on October 10 at the Golden Palace Convention Centre in Neyyattinkara. The event aims to bring together patients, families, caregivers, and healthcare professionals to recognize the importance of dignified, compassionate care for those with serious illnesses.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-09/pallium-india-celebrates-world-hospice-and-palliative-care-d.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Oncologist M.V. Pillai will inaugurate the program, which features cultural performances by the palliative care community. The gathering seeks to emphasize that palliative care is an essential component of modern healthcare while honoring the courage of patients and the dedication of their support networks.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief captures the essential details of the upcoming event accurately.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/kerala/world-hospice-and-palliative-care-day-to-be-celebrated-on-october-10/article71565100.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
