       <h1>Pebble Flow Electric Trailer Offers Tech-Integrated Camping</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#tech</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The $159,000 Pebble Flow electric RV aims to modernize the camping experience through integrated solar panels, electric motors, and automated hitching. The trailer features a minimalist interior with a convertible dinette and a Murphy bed that doubles as a dedicated workspace, providing a comfortable environment for remote work.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-09/pebble-flow-electric-trailer-offers-tech-integrated-camping.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Notable technology includes electrochromic &quot;smart glass&quot; windows that transition from clear to frosted for privacy. While the interior LED lighting and light-blocking windows create a spaceship-like atmosphere that obscures the time of day, the trailer provides a functional and luxe experience for users in real-world campsite conditions.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Effectively distills the tech features and user experience of the Pebble Flow.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.engadget.com/2282389/pebble-flow-ev-rv-review/" rel="noopener">Engadget</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
