       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-10-09 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Sitanshu Kotak Attributes Bhuvneshwar Kumar's T20I Recall to Experience</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#cricket</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>India batting coach Sitanshu Kotak has defended Bhuvneshwar Kumar’s return to the T20I squad for the upcoming New Zealand series, citing the need for veteran experience. Kotak noted that India’s recent bowling performance in England highlighted a reliance on Jasprit Bumrah, necessitating the inclusion of seasoned players.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-09/sitanshu-kotak-attributes-bhuvneshwar-kumars-t20i-recall-to-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Kumar’s recall follows two successful Indian Premier League seasons where he secured 48 wickets in 30 matches for Royal Challengers Bengaluru. Kotak emphasized that Kumar’s consistent domestic form and suitability for New Zealand conditions influenced the selection. Meanwhile, Kotak declined to comment on Mohammed Shami’s selection prospects, stating that such decisions remain solely with the selection panel.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the source's key points regarding the recall of Bhuvneshwar Kumar and the coach's comments on Shami.</p>
