     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-09 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Tamil Nadu Government Announces Major Administrative Reshuffle</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Tamil Nadu Home Secretary K. Manivasan has been transferred to the position of Commissioner of Land Administration. He is succeeded by A. Karthik, the former Chairman and Managing Director of the Tamil Nadu Small Industries Development Corporation (TANSIDCO). </p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-09/tamil-nadu-government-announces-major-administrative-reshuff.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>In related appointments, senior IPS officer Prem Anand Sinha has been named Director of the Vigilance and Anti-Corruption Directorate (DVAC). Additionally, Rajesh Lakhoni has been moved to lead TNEB and the Tamil Nadu Power Distribution Corporation Limited, while V. Arun Roy takes over as Secretary of Finance (Expenditure). These changes follow a series of strategic reassignments across the state’s administrative and police departments.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is accurate and covers the key personnel changes mentioned in the text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/tamil-nadu/tamil-nadu-home-secretary-tneb-chairman-transferred/article71562513.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
