     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-09 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>TPCC President Alleges BRS-BJP Collusion Over Electoral Roll Revision</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Telangana Pradesh Congress Committee president B. Mahesh Kumar Goud has accused the Bharat Rashtra Samithi (BRS) of maintaining silence regarding the Special Intensive Revision of electoral rolls due to a tacit understanding with the BJP. Goud alleged the BRS fears federal scrutiny into party leaders' wealth and ongoing investigations, such as the Kaleshwaram project case.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-09/tpcc-president-alleges-brs-bjp-collusion-over-electoral-roll.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Claiming that nearly 90 lakh votes are slated for removal in Telangana, Goud asserted that the Congress party will actively protect the rights of eligible voters. He criticized the BRS leadership for failing to challenge the Election Commission, contrasting their current stance with historical examples of fair electoral processes.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the political accusations and the context of the electoral roll controversy.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/telangana/brs-silent-on-sir-due-to-tacit-understanding-with-bjp-alleges-mahesh-goud/article71563891.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
