       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SCIENCE</span> · BBC Science · 2026-10-09 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Wales Businesses Face Workplace Recycling Challenges</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#science</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Despite the Welsh government's 2024 Workplace Recycling Law, only 61% of employees in Wales report recycling often at work. A lack of facilities and unclear labelling remain significant barriers, with 20% of workers recalling no recycling options at all. Experts suggest that centralizing waste collection and removing individual desk bins can improve compliance by mirroring home recycling habits.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-09/wales-businesses-face-workplace-recycling-challenges.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Some firms, such as recruitment agency Acorn by Synergie, have reported significant improvements after adopting these measures. While initial staff resistance is common, businesses find that consistent facilities and clear, centralized stations eventually make recycling a standard workplace practice, helping offset costs associated with landfill collections.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the workplace recycling challenges and the proposed solutions mentioned in the source.</p>
